@startuml sd_us117
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title US117 - Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "ATCC" as Actor
participant "Entry (Envoy)\nvirtual IP of aircraft-maintenance" as EAM
box "aircraft-maintenance-n (the replica that answers)" #F7F7F7
participant "MaintenanceController" as MaintenanceController
participant "ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase" as ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase
database "own database" as DBAM
end box
collections "peer replicas\naircraft-maintenance-m" as PAM
== GET /api/maintenance/records/hours ==
Actor -> EAM : GET /api/maintenance/records/hours\n(HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer JWT)
EAM -> MaintenanceController : to a ready replica\n(another one if it fails)
MaintenanceController -> ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase : execute(...)
ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase -> DBAM : own maintenance records
ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase -> PAM : GET /internal/replicas/maintenance-records\n(every peer in parallel)
PAM --> ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase : their maintenance records
ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase -> ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase : keep the latest change of each record,\nleave out deleted ones; filter, compute, sort, page
ViewTotalMaintenanceHoursInFleetUseCase --> MaintenanceController : result
MaintenanceController --> Actor : 200 OK (X-Node-Id; X-Partial-Result if both holders of a record were unreachable)
@enduml
